  "answer": "<p><strong>Correct Answers:</strong></p> <ul><li><strong>Set the source stage as CodeCommit, use CodeBuild for the build stage, and deploy with CloudFormation.</strong></li> <li><strong>Choose Bitbucket as the source, perform builds using CodeBuild, and handle deployment to Amazon ECS.</strong></li></ul> <p>AWS CodePipeline supports several popular code repositories as source stages, such as CodeCommit, GitHub, and Bitbucket. CodeBuild is a fully managed service designed to compile source code, run tests, and produce ready-to-deploy application packages, making it an excellent fit for the build stage in a Lambda CI/CD pipeline. For the deployment phase, CodePipeline integrates with services such as CloudFormation and Amazon ECS (when deploying to ECS). These combinations work natively with AWS and support automated deployments triggered by repository commits.</p> <p>The option <i>Utilize GitHub for the source, use Jenkins to build, and CodeDeploy to deploy the application</i> is incorrect because although CodeDeploy can deploy Lambda or EC2 applications, direct Jenkins integration needs external configurations and is not natively supported by CodePipeline for automated build steps in this context.</p> <p><i>Set CodeCommit as the source, opt for Travis CI in the build stage, and deploy via CloudFormation</i> is not valid since Travis CI is not natively integrated into AWS CodePipeline as a build provider; additional manual configuration or custom actions would be needed.</p> <p><i>Configure GitHub as source, build with Jenkins, and use CodeCommit for deployment</i> is incorrect because CodeCommit is a source code repository, not a deployment target; you cannot deploy applications using CodeCommit.</p> <p><strong>Tips:</strong> When designing CI/CD pipelines in AWS, leverage services with built-in AWS CodePipeline integration for optimal automation. This will minimize custom configurations and potential errors, enabling smoother continuous deployment workflows.</p>",
  "query": "<p>A development team is implementing microservices using AWS Lambda. They want to set up a CI/CD pipeline with AWS CodePipeline to automatically build and deploy Lambda applications each time a developer pushes new code to a git repository. Which combinations of pipeline stages and services are suitable for this purpose? <strong>(Choose TWO.)</strong></p>",
